{
  "_KIT_CLASS": "KIT \u2014 the opt-in harness wiring, as a shape. This file is JSON and has no comment syntax, so its classification marker is this KEY rather than a leading comment; process/EXTRACTION.md \u00a7 The one file classification convention states the carve-out.",
  "_README": "Kit template — copy to .claude/settings.json to ACTIVATE the Claude Code hooks (they execute shell commands on tool use / session start, so activation is a deliberate operator decision). The git-level commit-prefix guard (scripts/githooks/commit-msg) is wired separately via `git config core.hooksPath scripts/githooks` — kit-init.sh wires it ONCE at adoption and commits the hooks' executable bit, setup.sh re-wires and repairs it on EVERY fresh clone (process/contracts/initializer.md § 2) — and does NOT depend on this file.",

  "_NO_PLACEHOLDERS": "This file has NO <angle-bracket> tokens to fill in — copy it as it stands. The values a project declares live where they are USED — the adapter, scripts/config.sh and the commit-msg hook — and the self-test asserts that any <token> this file glosses appears in it.",

  "_WHAT_THIS_FILE_MAY_CONTAIN": "ONLY SETTINGS KEYS WHOSE EFFECT THE KIT CAN DEMONSTRATE: if the kit cannot show what a key does, the kit does not ship it. Add a key here only alongside the thing that reads it.",

  "_WHERE_THE_TRUNK_POLICY_ACTUALLY_LIVES": "The adapter (AGENTS.md) § 'The trunk, the branches, and what counts as code here', which cites process/MANUAL.md § The code-vs-metadata rule. Both are documents an agent actually reads; the rule is not copied here, because a third copy is what drifts.",

  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/scripts/hooks/require-role.sh\"" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/scripts/hooks/session-start.sh\"" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Notification": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/scripts/notify-hook.sh\"" }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
